# never wants a `node update-system.mjs apply` merge to restore. Read natively
# by apply() itself (see plans/07-31-26_replace-update-mechanism-with-merge.md):
# a modify/delete conflict on a listed path auto-resolves to "keep deleted",
# and a final unconditional sweep catches upstream adding a brand-new file
# under an excluded directory (which would otherwise auto-merge cleanly with
# no conflict at all, since there'd be nothing local to conflict with).
